cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Project FEAR: Fear-Enhanced Asymmetric Rewards for LLM Calibration and Abstention"
abstract: >-
  A research project investigating whether punishment-dominant asymmetric
  reinforcement-learning rewards improve confidence calibration, selective
  abstention, and judge capability in language models. The central result
  (Finding O) shows that under GRPO with within-group z-score advantage
  normalization, the reward design collapses to a single abstention-threshold
  dial: asymmetry changes how often the model abstains, not per-question
  calibration.
type: software
